# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# The Dockerfiles do a `COPY . .` in their build stage, so anything left in
# this list would be sent to the Docker daemon and copied into the image.
# That is slow, it inflates the image, and — worse — a host `node_modules`
# copied over a container one silently breaks the native bindings.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dependencies — the image installs its own, for the target platform.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Build output — the image builds from source.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
out
**/out
build
**/build
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo

# Tests and coverage.
coverage
**/coverage
.nyc_output
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
test-results
**/test-results
blob-report
**/blob-report
.playwright
**/.playwright

# VCS and CI — the build does not need the history.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local environment — real secrets must never enter a build layer.
# `.env.example` IS kept: the image's entrypoint may read it for documentation.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs and temporary files.
logs
**/*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.tmp
tmp
**/tmp

# The lockfile IS required: the Dockerfiles run `pnpm fetch --frozen-lockfile`.
# Excluding it breaks the reproducible, offline install.
